# New task: check ONE rule

Rule id: {{.ID}}
Severity: {{.Severity}}
Rule: {{.Text}}

Check only this rule. Ignore every other problem.
Report a violation only in lines the diff adds (lines starting with "+").

Work in these steps. Do not skip a step, and do not answer before step 3 is done.
1. Split the rule into its atomic requirements. A rule that lists several items (separated by ";", or
   pointing to a convention doc section) has one requirement per item. When the rule names a doc,
   take the items from that doc section in the first message.
2. For EACH requirement, walk EVERY added line of EVERY changed file it applies to.
   Example: for "one argument per line in multi-line calls", look at every call that spans lines;
   for "public functions before private", list the order of the added functions in each file.
3. Record one entry per requirement in "checks":
   - FAIL with the file:line and the added code that breaks it,
   - PASS with what you looked at (for example "12 multi-line calls in reader.go, all one per line"),
   - N/A when no added line is of that kind.
A PASS without "looked at" evidence is not accepted.

End with this JSON block. "findings" repeats every FAIL check, one per violating line:
```json
{"checks": [{"requirement": "one item of the rule", "status": "PASS or FAIL or N/A", "evidence": "file:line — code, or what you looked at"}],
 "verdict": "FAIL when any check is FAIL, else PASS",
 "findings": [{"file": "path", "line": 0, "message": "what breaks the rule"}]}
```
